  "averageRating" : 0,
  "category" : "Assessment and Accountability",
  "createdAt" : 1762383465,
  "description" : "This dataset is a summary of accountability data for public schools and districts from 2023 onward. It includes the overall classification, reason for classification, annual criterion-referenced target percentages and weights, accountability percentile, and cumulative criterion-referenced target percentage.\n\nAll Massachusetts public schools and districts with sufficient data are classified into one of two categories: schools and districts that require assistance or intervention, and schools and districts that do not require assistance or intervention. This dataset provides information on each district and school's performance against improvement targets and their overall performance compared to other schools in the state.\n\nAccountability percentiles are only calculated for schools, and are not available at the district level. For more information about school and district accountability classifications and the appropriate use of accountability data, please see the <a href=\"https://www.doe.mass.edu/accountability/lists-tools/default.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Accountability Lists, Materials, and Tools</a> page on the District and School Accountability website.\n\nThis dataset contains the same data that is also published on our DESE Profiles site: \n<a href=\"https://profiles.doe.mass.edu/statereport/accountability.aspx\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Accountability Report</a>",
